  "aboutParagraphs": [
    "Heritage Park is Olathe's heavily wooded test — 18 holes at par 54 across 5,009 feet, with the trees doing most of the talking and a little elevation adding character. It's a classic Kansas City-area park course that rewards clean, patient golf.",
    "Free to play with concrete tees and Mach X baskets, and very cart friendly despite the woods. The fairways are corridors, the greens are guarded, and the round is over before you want it to be.",
    "A friendly technical course that locals play weekly — bring a midrange you trust."
  ],
